# Normalise to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Windows is the development machine but the GPU box and the SQLite download
# run on Linux, and a shell script checked out with CRLF fails there with
# `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` -- which reads as a missing shell rather than a
# line ending. Keeping one convention everywhere avoids the whole class.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.npz binary
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
